 product of two functions $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)={3}^{x}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =(x)^{′}\\cdot {3}^{x}+x\\cdot ({3}^{x})^{′} \\\\  & ={3}^{x}+(x)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot {3}^{x}) \\\\  & ={3}^{x}+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot {3}^{x} \\\\  & =(1+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3){3}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287934 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1371ebf8-eb22-510a-8da9-ab71603cf224" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)x{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284960} {:answer/id #uuid "53d9fa80-4531-56fa-a24b-26f7f44fadfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285560} {:answer/id #uuid "7e63c504-8cfa-54d7-aead-931836c675c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(2{e}^{x}+x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285950} {:answer/id #uuid "8f418a4b-7d9e-52b0-a17c-229783a68355" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)x{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286094} {:answer/id #uuid "904ec37a-bb54-5997-a86e-3970a5f9817d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(x{e}^{x}+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286106}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1371ebf8-eb22-510a-8da9-ab71603cf224" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)x{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284960} :answer-field/id #uuid "4af7b461-8f62-58e4-ac36-73b94cae5741" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287310}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5d5b2e99-3a45-59ab-9bf2-0e86debf5990" :question/math-academy-id "q-1916" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={x}^{2}{e}^{x},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={x}^{2}$ and $v(x)={e}^{x}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =({x}